WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.739
If you want to hear about all the references
Annabelle: Creation has to the director’s

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.880
old YouTube videos, then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.020
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.180
On the last episode I preached about some
things you might have missed in the original

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.890
Annabelle -- so today, I’ll be putting together
the pieces of the 2017 prequel, Annabelle:

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:21.890
Creation.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.170
This episode is special because this is the
first time I’m covering a movie made by

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.170
a fellow YouTuber.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.660
This film was directed by David F Sandberg,
who goes by Ponysmasher on YouTube.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.890
His most well known video was Lights Out,
which got him the job to make the feature

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.570
film version; here’s a photo of me being
weird at the premiere at VidCon 2016.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.850
The lead actress of this film is Talitha Bateman,
who is the brother of Gabriel Bateman from

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:40.850
Lights Out.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.480
Annabelle: Creation opens with a shot of a
doll eyeball in Mr. Mullins’s toy shop.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.789
This image foreshadows the fate of his wife,
who lost her left eye after being attacked

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:50.560
by the demon and wears a porcelain mask to
cover it up.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.409
This sign for Mullins Toy Company describes
the figures as handcrafted fine dolls, and

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:57.010
we later see that there are only 100 of them
in existence.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.239
This is actually the director’s hand writing
the number 1 right here, he explains this

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:02.329
in the behind the scenes videos on his YouTube
channel.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:05.840
But I think this also helps answer a question
from the first one, which is why this particular

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.180
doll is so rare.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.330
The real life quote-on-quote “haunted”
doll described in the Warrens’ case files

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.800
is a common Raggedy Ann doll.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.620
The sign also says that this doll is available
at Palmeri’s Toy Shop, a reference to the

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.430
Palmeri Apartments in the original Annabelle.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.370
We’ve talked about how that original film
naturally drew some inspiration from the previous

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.580
king of creepy doll movies: Child’s Play
-- which I have a whole series of Things You

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.580
Missed videos on.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.720
I found the opening of this second Annabelle
film to be very reminiscent of the opening

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.800
of Child’s Play 2 -- both essentially showing
the creation of the doll.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.300
Mr. Mullins’s daughter, Bee, play hide and
seek with him, and her hiding spot is behind

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.760
the curtain by the window.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.031
After her death, the demon uses her likeness
on many occasions, which could explain why

00:01:41.031 --> 00:01:45.050
it hides in the same spot in Mia’s apartment
in Annabelle, and why it uses the record player

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.270
to mess with its victims.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.180
Twelve years after Bee’s death, the Mullinses
decide to take in a group of orphan girls

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.480
and we meet Linda and Janice on the bus ride
over.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.790
Uhh, she does know that that’s not red,
right?

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.930
The older girls in the front of the bus are
reading “Modern Teen” magazine and this

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.360
one’s REALLY into it.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.990
They arrive and meet Mr. Mullins, and the
front door of the house has both traditional

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:07.420
and inverted crosses, perhaps a clue about
the forces of good and evil at play beyond

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.420
these doors.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.409
When the girls tour the house, it’s one
big long tracking shot -- just like this shot

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:16.569
in The Conjuring -- which this movie is a
spin-off of and The Curse of La Llorona, or

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.069
as I call it Spanish The Conjuring -- also
a part of the series.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:23.879
In the Behind the Scenes videos, Ponysmasher
describes a shot that took 12 takes, and I’m

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:25.420
guessing this is it.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:30.510
“On Annabelle Creation, I think the most
we ever did was 12 takes, but that was for

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.719
a long steadycam shot with 8 different actors
and it was pretty complicated.”

00:02:35.719 --> 00:02:38.739
Mr. Mullins introduces Janice to the chairlift,
which is very slow.

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:41.240
I felt like I was waiting for King Zora to
get out of the way again.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.520
There’s also a brief moment where Bee’s
image can barelyyyy be seen in the background.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.459
During the night, Janice realizes the door
to Bee’s room is somehow unlocked, and wanders

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:01.950
in there against Mr. Mullins’s orders, where
she discovers that the Annabelle doll is locked

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.920
in the closet surrounded by Bible pages.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.370
After the closet door continues to open on
it’s own, she throws a blanket over the

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.370
doll.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.530
As she continues to explore the room, it comes
for her and corners her, but when the blanket

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.079
falls away, it’s revealed that there was
nothing underneath.

00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:18.019
This is a direct reference to David Sandberg’s
short film Attic Panic, on the Ponysmasher

00:03:18.019 --> 00:03:19.000
YouTube Channel.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.989
Later in the movie, when the teenage girl
Carol gets stuck in the barn, there’s another

00:03:32.989 --> 00:03:36.150
idea lifted from Attic Panic, which is the
lightbulb unscrewing itself.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.500
Considering how many feature films have stolen
his concept from Lights Out, I’m glad he

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.459
was able to use this stuff from Attic Panic
before somebody else did.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.840
He also got the orchestra to include a cover
of the simple soundtrack he created for the

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.840
short.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.541
This would not be the only reference to his
own shorts in the movie.

00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:53.579
The Nun who is in charge of all the girls
is named Sister Charlotte, and in one scene

00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:57.120
she shows Mr. Mullins a photograph of her
time in Romania, where he points out an older

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.400
Nun in the background that she doesn’t recognize.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.620
This is actually Valak, the Nun demon and the antagonist of The Conjuring 2 and of

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.920
course The Nun, which Annabelle: Creation’s
post credits scene is a teaser for.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.040
In the scene where the two older girls are
gossiping under the sheet and they’re attacked

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:30.840
by something, they end up saying that it looked
like Mrs. Mullins, but if you actually pause

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.889
on that moment, it doesn’t look like her
or her mask, it just appears to be a generic

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:36.280
porcelain mask with dark eyes.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.330
It kind of gives me The Purge vibes.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.900
Maybe this image will be expanded on in another
movie.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.889
Janice discovers a picture of Bee in the hallway
and brings it into her room to look at it.

00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:48.479
When she puts it in a dark spot the eyes give
off a demonic glow, and this same effect is

00:04:48.479 --> 00:04:50.960
used later on when we see the possessed form
of Janice.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.930
This is the same effect that is used throughout
Sandberg’s feature film version of Lights

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.340
Out on the main antagonist, Diana.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.139
There are a number of visuals that reference
Bee.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:01.710
Bee is a nickname that the Mullins had given
their daughter which is short for her full

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.710
name: Annabelle.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.580
I think this might be an intentional parallel
to the first film where we constantly see

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.780
the letter A. In this one, there’s an image
of a Bee on the window in her old room, Bees

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.470
on the vertical posts holding up the railing
alongside the stairs, and when Linda looks

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.280
through this kaleidoscope, this is what she
sees, which is similar to the stereotypical

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.620
Hollywood interpretation of what a Bee’s
point of view might look like.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.139
I looked up and they don’t actually see
a bunch of repeat images -- that only in the

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:25.139
movies.

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:26.860
Remember that slow chair I mentioned earlier?

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.350
You didn’t think that wasn’t going to
come back did you?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.830
In fact, I think the scene where the chair
gets stuck with Janice on it and the demon

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.640
lurking nearby, is another throwback to the
original Annabelle, where Mia gets stuck on

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.440
the elevator, that won’t go up with the
demon lurking about in the storage area.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.741
When we learn the story of how the doll essentially
got possessed, it’s also very similar to

00:05:43.741 --> 00:05:46.889
what happened to the nurses after the events
of Annabelle, with the demon pretending to

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:50.289
be the spirit of a little girl named Annabelle,
asking permission to move into the doll and

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:51.599
then causing violent attacks.

00:05:51.599 --> 00:05:55.131
The little girl Linda realizes that there
is something evil in the doll and tries to

00:05:55.131 --> 00:05:59.259
get rid of it by throwing it into the well
in the middle of the night and… well…

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:00.680
this happens.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.520
*scream* "No, no!" *scream*

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.600
It’s another callback to one of the short
films on David’s channel, this one a 2014

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.920
flick called Coffer.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.000
Roll it.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.960
So we find out how Mrs. Mullins was injured,
by the demon posing as their daughter’s

00:06:29.979 --> 00:06:34.539
ghost, but it’s too late, because the demon
Malthus gets to both Mr. and Mrs. Mullins,

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:36.490
causing the girls to try to escape the house.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:40.000
They get into the car, but have some trouble
starting it, causing the headlights to blink

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.840
on and off, and they notice the scarecrow
move between light flashes, which is of course

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.400
a callback to Lights Out.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.120
At the end of the day, Sister Charlotte is
able to lock the demonically (is that word?)

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.320
demonically possessed Janice in the closet,
where she disappears through the wall, but

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.580
the other girls are safe at least.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:07.471
They put the doll, which has supposedly been
purged of all evil by this dude, in the back

00:07:07.471 --> 00:07:11.350
of the police car, which drives away past
the grave of Bee, where this all started.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:14.810
So this goes back to that whole question from
the last video -- how did the doll go from

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.080
this cop car to John purchasing it and giving
to Mia?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.780
The demon Malthus has to have something to
do with it.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.770
Our final sequence takes place at St. Joachim
Orphanage.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:27.490
Joachim is a reference not only to one of
the great Bulls players of the 2000s but also

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:31.229
a Biblical reference to the father of Mary,
which makes sense because of the themes of

00:07:31.229 --> 00:07:34.770
their church vs. the evil demons that persist
throughout this franchise.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:39.280
The woman working at the orphanage is Lotta
Losten, the wife of David Sandberg; she stars

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.280
in…

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.539
I think ALL of his short films and cameos
in all of his features.

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:45.949
The Higgins family, who you’ll remember
from the original Annabelle, come to adopt

00:07:45.949 --> 00:07:49.889
Janice, who turns out to be their daughter
who comes back to kill them as a sacrifice

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:51.270
for Malthus years later.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.910
When they first meet her, they give her a
gift.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.719
It’s an actual Raggedy Ann doll, yet another
parallel to the original Annabelle, which

00:07:56.719 --> 00:07:59.169
also has this doll featured in it’s epilogue.

00:07:59.169 --> 00:08:03.189
If you were to visit the actual Warren museum,
this is the doll you’d find in the glass

00:08:03.189 --> 00:08:04.189
case.

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:07.800
Annabelle: Creation ends as many Conjurverse
movies do with a slow push in on the central

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.030
object of this movie, in this case, of course,
the Annabelle doll.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:14.699
So we’ve seen Annabelle’s past, we’ve
seen Annabelle’s origin, so join me next

00:08:14.699 --> 00:08:18.150
time on Things You Missed to see Annabelle’s
future, because we’re going to be covering

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.280
the newest film, Annabelle Comes Home.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:24.360
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld so you don’t
miss it, make sure you ring that deathbell

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.069
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:08:27.069 --> 00:08:29.349
Assuming we both survive.

